\"To date several randomized controlled trials (RCT) have shown that pelvic floor muscle (PFM) training is effective in 
the treatment of female stress (SUI) and mixed urinary incontinence and, therefore, it is recommended as a first-line   
therapy. While the effectiveness of treatment is established, there are different theoretical rationales for why PFM    
