### 3. Additional context (if relevant):                                                                                
The screening process involved careful application of the PICOTS framework: Population (women with SUI/UUI/MUI),        
Intervention (PFMT), Comparison (no treatment/placebo/sham/inactive control), Outcome (not strictly required for        
title/abstract screening but considered), Study design (RCT/q-RCT). Studies were excluded only when they clearly lacked 
an RCT/q-RCT design, PFMT intervention arm, or appropriate control arm. Four studies were excluded with high confidence 
(terminology reports, observational surveys, pharmacology chapter, guidelines). Three studies were included with low    
confidence due to being reviews (studies 54, 63) or having ambiguous control/population (study 56). The remaining seven 
studies were included with high or medium confidence as they clearly met all criteria. The total numbers reflect this   
chunk only (14 studies). The review's focus on PFMT vs inactive control for UI in women was consistently applied. Note  
that study 20's physical therapy intervention was considered to include PFMT as a core component for UI treatment, which
is consistent with the review's scope.                                                                                  
                                                                                                                        
